IMPORT prelude

-- snap3 HELPERS: three-valued logic over MAYBE BOOLEAN, used by every snap3 module.
-- These are not provisions of the Act, so their names carry the part's own label `snap3` (no other part uses it)
-- instead of a section label. Nothing here is law: it is the plumbing that lets a rule say "every one of these holds"
-- without turning NOTHING (the text does not say) into FALSE (the text says no).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no, in its own words
--   NOTHING     the text does not say (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording)

-- All of the conditions hold: one JUST FALSE makes it JUST FALSE; all JUST TRUE makes it JUST TRUE; otherwise NOTHING.
-- An empty list is JUST TRUE (nothing is required).
GIVEN `the conditions` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`snap3 every one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN c YIELD c EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the conditions` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF all (GIVEN c YIELD c EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the conditions` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- At least one of the conditions holds: one JUST TRUE makes it JUST TRUE; all JUST FALSE makes it JUST FALSE; otherwise NOTHING.
-- An empty list is JUST FALSE (nothing holds).
GIVEN `the conditions` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`snap3 at least one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN c YIELD c EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the conditions` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF all (GIVEN c YIELD c EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the conditions` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The opposite: JUST TRUE becomes JUST FALSE and the reverse; NOTHING stays NOTHING.
GIVEN `the condition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`snap3 the opposite of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the condition`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (NOT b)

-- A plain yes-or-no fact the person states, as an answer.
GIVEN `the fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`snap3 the person states` MEANS JUST `the fact`

#ASSERT `snap3 every one of these holds` (LIST JUST TRUE, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `snap3 every one of these holds` (LIST JUST TRUE, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `snap3 every one of these holds` (LIST JUST TRUE, NOTHING, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `snap3 every one of these holds` EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `snap3 at least one of these holds` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `snap3 at least one of these holds` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `snap3 at least one of these holds` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `snap3 at least one of these holds` EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `snap3 the opposite of` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `snap3 the opposite of` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `snap3 the opposite of` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `snap3 the person states` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
